ifficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a005f1b5-54c0-59d7-8a93-206dab6e0652" :question/math-academy-id "q-77146" :question/problem "![](images/fe/fec5c3e96eeed9fb01479c0127e2d530a628855a124d8ab1ef380c48c2f569f1.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $LMNL,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the counterclockwise direction?" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in counterclockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={C}_{1}\\cup \\{-{C}_{2}\\}\\cup {C}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{2}$ is the same path as ${C}_{2}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179669 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5ce5418-6b75-5efa-b7f9-99ee16c510be" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Line Integral of a Vector-Valued Function Along a Union of Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cc09296-8638-5bb9-aa09-d659533f54b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342737} {:answer/id #uuid "4f83c7c3-3dd2-503c-84e2-cff8e0497ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342899} {:answer/id #uuid "84da968a-d353-52cb-9a5b-8037954b3f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343377} {:answer/id #uuid "b500e96e-2b58-5d83-8ee1-056f5152c148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343823} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c60230-d8a1-5d13-ba1f-f00ed01733ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b500e96e-2b58-5d83-8ee1-056f5152c148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343823} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe814ee1-ffa1-535f-9662-cd673e89b2c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60807a56-8605-5f52-976b-4c6cebda8f0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-77185" :question/problem "![](images/c0/c0a4f042748ddadd824bed4ee71bca9724d7ca7dcc376a0ccf7c1353d59ec4fc.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(-2,2)$ to the point $B(-1,2),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $B(-1,2)$ to the point $D(-1,0).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-\\frac{7}{2},$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(x-y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j,$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the first integral, so we only need to work out the second.\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the vertical line segment from $B$ to $D.$ It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}(t) & =b+t(d-b) \\\\  & =⟨-1,2⟩+t(⟨-1,0⟩-⟨-1,2⟩) \\\\  & =⟨-1,2-2t⟩ \\\\  & =-\\,i+(2-2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<1.$ Along this segment, we have $x=-1$ and $y=2-2t.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t)) & =(x-y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j \\\\  & =(-1-(2-2t))\\,i+(2-2t-(-1))\\,j \\\\  & =(-3+2t)\\,i+(3-2t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-2t)j \\\\  & =-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =((-3+2t)\\,i+(3-2t)\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\,j) \\\\  & =(3-2t)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4t-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{1}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4t-6)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2}+[2{t}^{2}-6t]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2}+[2({1}^{2})-6(1)-0] \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2}-4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179669 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5ce5418-6b75-5efa-b7f9-99ee16c510be" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Line Integral of a Vector-Valued Function Along a Union of Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ccbd978-8163-5c7e-baae-b8ad95985a86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342350} {:answer/id #uuid "453e49ec-25af-50ef-847c-f9e8f100fa90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342807} {:answer/id #uuid "78d2918a-06f4-5e2f-8f95-8ce2e0a1d53e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343281} {:answer/id #uuid "7c924cb2-9540-5923-aef1-54902d61b6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343312} {:answer/id #uuid "a953ff99-deba-55f2-9b54-5b5b5650e514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ccbd978-8163-5c7e-baae-b8ad95985a86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342350} :answer-field/id #uuid "10c5cc9a-ab7f-5bd2-8f67-b0bc3b91ae44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8fc56ee5-fc5d-5429-bfdb-4254f7ee30fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-77191" :question/problem "![](images/04/0457cb819e6f39ef9c0978e356cff788e1cf5edbef9cbf844a054ab777b70eac.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a the line segment from the point $A(-2,0)$ to the point $B(0,1),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of the line segment from the point $B(0,1)$ to the point $D(1,1).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-\\frac{3}{2},$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(x-2y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j,$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the second integral, so we only need to work out the first.\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is the line segment from $A$ to $B.$  It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}(t) & =a+t(b-a) \\\\  & =⟨-2,0⟩+t(⟨0,1⟩-⟨-2,0⟩) \\\\  & =⟨-2+2t,t⟩ \\\\  & =(-2+2t)i+t\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<1.$ Along this segment, we have $x=-2+2t$ and $y=t.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t)) & =(x-2y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j \\\\  & =((-2+2t)-2t)\\,i+(t-(-2+2t))\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\,i+(2-t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2+2t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =2\\,i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =(-2\\,i+(2-t)\\,j)\\cdot (2\\,i+j) \\\\  & =-2-t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t+(-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2-t)\\,\\text{d}t-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & ={[-2t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =[-2(1)-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-0]-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415770 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179669 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5ce5418-6b75-5efa-b7f9-99ee16c510be" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Line Integral of a Vector-Valued Function Along a Union of Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "126d13a7-71fa-5051-a4a2-28f29e56cf03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415734} {:answer/id #uuid "2216ca5d-6c6a-5107-a068-323114e3fc15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415735} {:answer/id #uuid "7aae6b46-36e9-538a-8e22-b5381b749d2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415746} {:answer/id #uuid "7e44c518-6f87-55b7-bbc1-4434ed19cb47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415747} {:answer/id #uuid "8ea13c33-b0aa-51a8-a9cd-a56c81fb144a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e44c518-6f87-55b7-bbc1-4434ed19cb47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415747} :answer-field/id #uuid "7adcd9af-5265-5496-ada0-3911ecad9cdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415766}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3412530f-81b3-51bb-95a9-4599a55eb207" :question/math-academy-id "q-77250" :question/problem "![](images/87/87182d625f4e669a6b2791a17f3e12c34922043b8f3deefd6b2473e8fb529886.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(2,0),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a section of the parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ from the point $A(2,0)$ to the point $B(0,4).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2,$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=x\\,i$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the first integral, so we only need to work out the second.\n\nLet ${C}_{2}$ be the section of parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ from $A$ to $B.$ Then,\n $-{C}_{2}$ will be the same path but travelled from $B$ to $A.$ The path $-{C}_{2}$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}(t)=t\\,i+(4-{t}^{2})\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<2.$ Along this curve, we have $x=t$ and $y=4-{t}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t)) & =x\\,i=t\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4-{t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i-2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =(t\\,i)\\cdot (i-2t\\,j) \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =2-{\\int }_{0}^{2}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2-{\\int }_{0}^{2}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2-{[\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2-[\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
